/*
 * ip_l4_proto_table.inc — shared Layer-4 dispatch table for the IPv4 and
 * IPv6 next-protocol classifiers (issue #238, F-CLEAN-005).
 *
 * Maps an IANA IP protocol number (0-255) to the internal PROTO_* id. It
 * replaces the two near-duplicate ~800-line switch statements that used to
 * live in ip_classify_next_proto() (proto_ip.c) and ip6_classify_next_proto()
 * (proto_ipv6.c); entries not listed stay at PROTO_UNKNOWN, which preserves
 * the old default: arm of both switches.
 *
 * Two entries are IPv4-only in the original code and are masked back to
 * PROTO_UNKNOWN by the IPv6 caller: 2 (IGMP) and 94 (IPIP -> PROTO_IP).
 *
 * This file is intentionally not include-guarded: it is included at the
 * single use site in each of the two .c files, where it emits one
 * file-local `static const` array (same pattern as proto_init_list.def).
 */

